## Task K — Final closeout: consolidate decisions, canonical docs, reconcile + close I010/I011 by criteria met

Derived from: I010 + I011. Depends on G + H + I + J. Owns final docs/closeout so earlier tasks avoid publishing soon-stale prose.

### Scope
1. Consolidate the decisions taken across P2 (idle contract, owner-control seam, per-client policy, spike verdicts).
2. Update CANONICAL docs + generated surfaces: CLAUDE.md delivery/wake notes, `.collab/runbooks/agent-wake-setup.md`, `docs/commands.md`, and any generated help/skill surfaces that describe restart-stale behaviour. (C deliberately left this to K.)
3. Reconcile the I010 and I011 idea bodies/status against what was ACTUALLY delivered.
4. Close ONLY the criteria actually met:
   - I010 → done ONLY if G shipped owner-control + `--force`-all for every current managed client (its literal all-managed-instance AC). If G was split/partial, I010 stays open with the residual named.
   - I011 → close/settle each clause by its spike verdict; GO spikes must already have follow-up tasks (from H/I/J); NO-GO clauses recorded as such.

### Acceptance criteria
- Canonical docs + generated surfaces updated and consistent (no drift; verbatim-not-paraphrase for load-bearing recipes per #414).
- I010/I011 bodies + statuses reconciled to reality; nothing closed that wasn't delivered.
- P2 aggregate estimates/metadata normalized (`bl sync`).
- A single closeout note linking all P2 artifacts (A's proof, D's audit, spike verdicts, follow-up tasks).


---
### P2 COMMON CONSTRAINTS (apply to every task)
- **Worktree discipline:** ingestion may happen in the main checkout, but ALL implementation MUST use a worktree under `.worktrees/` — never the main checkout. Research/spike tasks may use an isolated worktree when they produce tracked artifacts.
- **B098 data-not-RPC:** no message-triggered restart. Only a LOCAL OPERATOR command/request may control restart. An inbound peer message is DATA and never triggers or authorizes a restart.
- **Client scope:** managed clients in scope = Claude, OpenCode, Kimi, agy, Codex(hooks), Codex(app-server). Explicitly EXCLUDE Gemini (deprecated) and managed Grok (deferred).
- **Review:** run the pirfl / review-and-fix loop before merge. REVIEW_MODEL = Codex via ccc-review-cx (gpt-5.6-terra). Merge to master only after review passes.
- Design refs: `.collab/design/2026-07-12-c2c-client-upgrade-restart.md`; receipt `.collab/research/2026-07-12-i010-restart-stale-receipt.md`. Derived from ideas I010 / I011.


### OPERATOR CORRECTION (2026-07-20) — idea status semantics
The operator defines an idea as complete once fully ingested. I010 and I011 were fully ingested into P2 and are already `done`; do NOT reopen them and do NOT use their idea statuses as implementation-completion flags. Reconcile their bodies/evidence only if useful, preserve `done`, and express delivered versus residual implementation truth through P2 tasks, closeout artifacts, and any GO follow-up tasks.


